lose in either direction.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 53 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Tom Barrett (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Michigan's 7th District is an even partisan split, and first-term Republican Tom Barrett is defending the Lansing-area seat against Democrat William Lawrence in what raters treat as one of the House's closest contests. Five of ten expert ratings call it a Tossup, while the rest lean toward a Democratic flip, and prediction markets give the Democrat roughly a 57 to 61 percent chance.\n\nBarrett has a large fundraising advantage, with over $6.3 million raised and $2.9 million on hand, but outside groups have spent heavily against him while supporting Lawrence. Polling is sparse and dated, with the only recent head-to-head showing a narrow Democratic lead. Headlines highlight Barrett's public disagreement with Trump on a war issue and Lawrence's profile as a progressive climate candidate, keeping the race volatile heading into the final weeks.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6879, "margin": 2.86}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6475, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7011, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6783, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6189, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6168, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6888, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7095, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6925, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7073, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7167, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7145, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7121, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6654, "margin": 3.2}]}